{"name":"Residential gas furnace fault code lookup by brand","description":"What the flashing-LED or displayed fault code on a residential gas furnace's integrated control board means, taken from each manufacturer's own manual. A furnace tech reads a blink pattern or a short alphanumeric code off the control board and needs the manufacturer-specific meaning before touching anything; the code alone (e.g. '13', 'A033_F') means nothing without knowing whose board it is. Codes look alike across brands and mean different things: 13 is a limit switch lockout on a Carrier 58MVP and a blower/OEM mismatch on a Trane S8V2. Each record is one fault code from one brand's control board: the code as the board displays it, and the fault the manual names beside it. The corrective procedure is not reproduced here; the linked manual has it. No single source publishes this across brands because each manufacturer's control board firmware defines its own code set independently.","url":"https://referencesource.org/residential-furnace-fault-codes-by-brand/","licence":"factual compilation from manufacturer technical manuals","last_verified":"2026-08-28","stale_after":"2028-08-27","sources":["http://www.graycoolingman.com/uploads/1/0/6/6/10667336/carrier_variable-speed_2-stage_troubleshooting.pdf","https://airmanagementsupply.com/documents/rheem-ruud_R802V_UH_installation_instructions.pdf","https://elibrary.tranetechnologies.com/public/residential-hvac/Literature/Installation%20Operation%20and%20Maintenance/FNR-SVX003A-EN_10312025.pdf"],"records":[{"brand":"Carrier","model_series":"58MVP","fault_code":"11","fault_name":"NO FAULT IN RECENT HISTORY DISPLAY","id":"58mvp-carrier-11","url":"https://referencesource.org/residential-furnace-fault-codes-by-brand/58mvp-carrier-11/","source":"http://www.graycoolingman.com/uploads/1/0/6/6/10667336/carrier_variable-speed_2-stage_troubleshooting.pdf","source_quote":"Fault Code 11 NO FAULT IN RECENT HISTORY DISPLAY","verified_fields":["brand","fault_code"